Write a function gcd_or_dc that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers a and b and returns gcd(a, b) when a is greater than b, and the number of decimal digits of b otherwise. Write and use a helper function gcd(a, b) that returns the greatest common divisor by repeated remainders (gcd(a, 0) = a, gcd(0, 0) = 0). Write and use a helper function digcount(n) that returns how many decimal digits n has (1 for n = 0).
